All 15 tests pass. Here's what was implemented across two files:

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now checks for a missing/invalid `X-API-Key` header and raises HTTP 401 with a descriptive message, or returns the mapped username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — five changes:

| Endpoint | What changed |
|---|---|
| `GET /tasks` | Added `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` optional query filters, plus `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20, max 100) pagination. All filters combinable. |
| `POST /tasks` | New endpoint. Requires auth. Validates `project_id` exists (404 if not). Auto-generates integer ID via `max(...) + 1`. Returns 201 with the created task. |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | New endpoint. Requires auth. Partial update via `TaskUpdate` (only non-`None` fields applied). Returns 404 if task not found. |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | New endpoint. Requires auth. Returns 204 on success, 404 if not found. |

All endpoints follow the existing patterns (in-memory list storage, same status codes, `Depends(require_api_key)` for auth).
